# Three parked tasks this batch: LJ-1.440 (no-match), LJ-1.443 (launch),
# LJ-1.444 (launch).
#
# 1. LJ-1.440, no-match, seven reaccepts (accept-1 through accept-7, all
#    identical: exit_code 0, obligations_delta 0, obligations_open 1,
#    changed_files = [lj-1.440-report.md, review-of-sq-trunc-closed.md]).
#    No row in dev/pod/table.toml can match it and none should be written:
#    the brief itself cannot be satisfied by any return that takes the stop
#    path it orders. THE BRIEF REPAIR REQUEST BELOW NAMES THE CHECK.
#
#    agents/tasks/LJ-1-440/LJ-1.440.md:19-20 orders a D-10 stop: "READ
#    `agents/tasks/LJ-1-437/lj-1.437-report.md` BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE. IF
#    THAT FILE DOES NOT EXIST, OR ITS VERDICT IS NOT `GO`, WRITE NOTHING AND
#    STOP." The coder's worktree HEAD (ea04f35) predates LJ-1.437's report
#    landing in the main tree, so the file was absent there and the stop
#    fired: report at .pod-state/worktrees/LJ-1-440/agents/tasks/LJ-1-440/
#    lj-1.440-report.md:12 ("## D-10, BEFORE ANY AGDA") and :81 ("Measured
#    seconds: 0. No Agda process started."). No Agda ran, so exit_code is 0.
#
#    dev/pod/table.toml:4230-4242, row `task-lj-1-440-no-go-stated`
#    (admitted from the brief's own `no-go-stated` branch), requires
#    `exit_code = 42`. That code is Agda's own not-in-scope exit
#    (scripts/pod/witness.py:23, :310-311): it can only be produced by
#    running Agda against a witness. A D-10 stop that fires before any Agda
#    runs can never produce it. The branch and the stop clause that sits in
#    the SAME brief cannot both be satisfied by one return: `no-go-stated`
#    is unreachable on this path, by construction, not by bad luck.
#
#    THE SAME TEMPLATE IS IN THREE OTHER BRIEFS FROM THE SAME REFILL, so this
#    is a pattern and not a one-off: agents/tasks/LJ-1-442/LJ-1.442.md:207-214,
#    agents/tasks/LJ-1-443/LJ-1.443.md:222-229 and
#    agents/tasks/LJ-1-444/LJ-1.444.md:226-233 each carry an identical
#    `no-go-stated` branch (`exit_code = 42`) beside a `BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE
#    ... WRITE NOTHING AND STOP` D-10 clause of their own. None of the three
#    has hit it yet (442 is RUNNING; 443 and 444 are launch-parked on 442's
#    write scope, unrelated to this shape), so this batch names LJ-1.440
#    only and asks the mathematician to check the other three while repairing
#    it, rather than guessing their fix from here.
#
#    I am not proposing what the repaired branch should say. Deciding
#    whether a D-10 report-missing stop earns `escalate` to
#    `mathematician_adversarial`, a different action, or a new outcome
#    entirely is mathematics (AD3), not a row I can write from a measured
#    record: the branch table itself is what needs to change, and only the
#    mathematician can write into a brief.
#
# 2. LJ-1.443, launch, 0 changed files, exit_code None. Dispatch was REFUSED
